{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04UY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\CH_*(\\mathcal{X})$", "MATH_0003": "$k$", "MATH_0004": "$\\phi : \\mathcal{X} \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$\\CH_*(\\mathcal{X}) \\to \\CH_k(Y)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9523902357982af768874187b356cda95ea61bb719743fa84f535b2db4d8fe2a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eb1001acf8cf2f6fe0a96fd66e43513e6e8ec99abc2494a45e0ee4d5f05a2a09", "source_text": "This paper develops the foundations for intersection theory with rational coefficients for Deligne-Mumford stacks. If <MATH_0001> is a separated Deligne-Mumford stack, the chow group <MATH_0002> with rational coefficients is defined as the free abelian group of integral closed substacks of dimension <MATH_0003> up to rational equivalence. There is a flat pullback, a proper push-forward and a generalized Gysin homomorphism for regular local embeddings. If <MATH_0004> is a moduli space (ie. a proper morphism with is bijective on geometric points), there is an induced push-forward <MATH_0005> which is an isomorphism.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf8b74f75b04510f06bad679eac475e7a96757a7ec314d168e91e6831e8f83d6", "unit_id": "tag:04UY:item001-quote"}
